(5372680, 773300, 30049, '<td valign="top">Wonderful use of natural light.  I like that this photo can stand on it''s own in this challenge based on the challenge theme.  You really didn''t need to repeat the word "hope" in the title... 9</td>', 'Wonderful use of natural light.  I like that this photo can stand on it''s own in this challenge based on the challenge theme.  You really didn''t need to repeat the word "hope" in the title... 9', '2009-03-16 08:52:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(5372687, 773059, 30049, '<td valign="top">Amazing how long it takes...this image IMO is symbolic of "hope".  The building cranes give a strong sense of something rising.  Unique, and well seen, take on this challenge.</td>', 'Amazing how long it takes...this image IMO is symbolic of "hope".  The building cranes give a strong sense of something rising.  Unique, and well seen, take on this challenge.', '2009-03-16 08:54:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(5372718, 773766, 48820, '<td valign="top">I think she''ll get noticed.  I HOPE my wife doesn''t notice me noticing.</td>', 'I think she''ll get noticed.  I HOPE my wife doesn''t notice me noticing.', '2009-03-16 09:04:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(5372720, 773808, 30049, '<td valign="top">With the portrait orientation of this image the only part of this I saw was the robin and the wood - no title (too far down).  My first thought was "hopes of spring", because when we see robins, spring is near!<br/> <br/>Honestly, I was a tad disappointed to see that you felt the need to include "hope" in the title once I scrolled down...that''s what the challenge theme is.  The photo told a good story without feeding the challenge theme to the voters via the title.<br/> <br/>Back to the photo...the colors are strong, details in the bird are "ok", the wood stump is a little hot (slightly overexposed).  Perhaps slightly over sharpened. Compositionally you could lose a little off the bottom of this and give the robin more impact.<br/> <br/>All of the above is JMO of course. :-)  Good luck in the challenge. 5</td>', 'With the portrait orientation of this image the only part of this I saw was the robin and the wood - no title (too far down).  My first thought was "hopes of spring", because when we see robins, spring is near! Honestly, I was a tad disappointed to see that you felt the need to include "hope" in the title once I scrolled down...that''s what the challenge theme is.  The photo told a good story without feeding the challenge theme to the voters via the title. Back to the photo...the colors are strong, details in the bird are "ok", the wood stump is a little hot (slightly overexposed).  Perhaps slightly over sharpened. Compositionally you could lose a little off the bottom of this and give the robin more impact. All of the above is JMO of course. :-)  Good luck in the challenge. 5', '2009-03-16 09:05:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(5372737, 773014, 48820, '<td valign="top">I love this picture.  Hope is a stretch but I can see it.</td>', 'I love this picture.  Hope is a stretch but I can see it.', '2009-03-16 09:13:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(5372743, 773490, 54645, '<td valign="top">I like the high contrast. I''m not sure about the choice of tone, does not generate a sense of hope for me, more bleak.</td>', 'I like the high contrast. I''m not sure about the choice of tone, does not generate a sense of hope for me, more bleak.', '2009-03-16 09:15:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(5372753, 773444, 99218, '<td valign="top">really nice shot! i like it!</td>', 'really nice shot! i like it!', '2009-03-16 09:19:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(5372812, 773301, 3102, '<td valign="top">This is one of those places where the time of day can make a dramatic difference in the shot.  I''m guessing this was probably shot mid-day sometime.<br/> <br/>If you live near Sedona and can get back to shoot the Chapel of the Holy Cross just before sunset, it really makes for a more dramatic shot with warmer colors (or you could try bumping up the temperature to warm the colors of this, too).<br/> <br/>If you were to walk up Chapel Road toward the church entrance just a bit further, you can get a really cool backdrop of the mountain behind it, too.</td>', 'This is one of those places where the time of day can make a dramatic difference in the shot.  I''m guessing this was probably shot mid-day sometime. If you live near Sedona and can get back to shoot the Chapel of the Holy Cross just before sunset, it really makes for a more dramatic shot with warmer colors (or you could try bumping up the temperature to warm the colors of this, too). If you were to walk up Chapel Road toward the church entrance just a bit further, you can get a really cool backdrop of the mountain behind it, too.', '2009-03-16 09:39:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(5372821, 773229, 30049, '<td valign="top">This is nearly perfect (don''t like theme being repeated in title - this photo would have stood up fine without it).  Great setting, the silhouette is right on the mark, and the tall grass is a bonus.  Well done! 9</td>', 'This is nearly perfect (don''t like theme being repeated in title - this photo would have stood up fine without it).  Great setting, the silhouette is right on the mark, and the tall grass is a bonus.  Well done! 9', '2009-03-16 09:44:32.000000', NULL, 1),
