(5396333, 773849, 61961, '<td valign="top">Kevin, I thought this might be yours.  It''s an exceptionally clever concept.  The tiles look great against the black background.  The "letterbox" frame looks terrific (I almost think they should be outlawed). :-)  This would make a great poster and could possibly sell, but I think you would have to reshoot because even at this size it looks a bit soft.  I''d love to <i>really</i> see the grain in the wooden tiles!  I also felt the title was proselytizing, but didn''t "deduct" points for that.</td>', 'Kevin, I thought this might be yours.  It''s an exceptionally clever concept.  The tiles look great against the black background.  The "letterbox" frame looks terrific (I almost think they should be outlawed). :-)  This would make a great poster and could possibly sell, but I think you would have to reshoot because even at this size it looks a bit soft.  I''d love to really see the grain in the wooden tiles!  I also felt the title was proselytizing, but didn''t "deduct" points for that.', '2009-03-23 09:11:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(5396368, 773298, 61961, '<td valign="top">Jon, welcome to DPC.  I think the colors in this entry are beautiful.  The fact they come from spaghetti sauce packaging makes me happy.  Your image might have scored higher except people are very tired of water drop photos.  There are other subjects that get photographed more often, but for some reason people really hate the splash shots!<br/> <br/>I look forward to seeing your future entries.  And yes, those black dots along the bottom do mar the photo a bit.  As <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=98339" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Ja-9</a> suggested, check for sensor dust.</td>', 'Jon, welcome to DPC.  I think the colors in this entry are beautiful.  The fact they come from spaghetti sauce packaging makes me happy.  Your image might have scored higher except people are very tired of water drop photos.  There are other subjects that get photographed more often, but for some reason people really hate the splash shots! I look forward to seeing your future entries.  And yes, those black dots along the bottom do mar the photo a bit.  As  Ja-9 suggested, check for sensor dust.', '2009-03-23 09:42:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(5396369, 773444, 24454, '<td valign="top">Awesome, Enzo!  It is a beautiful photo.  The kind that stirs my heart and the kind of photography that I am passionate about.  But it is even a more beautiful story of what you are doing in the Philippines.  I sponsor an "adopted" little girl in the Philippines that I''ve been supporting since she was 3, and she''s almost old enough to be graduated from the program now, so I always have had a special interest in the Philippines, and wish someday I could go there myself.   I''m glad you won first place with this wonderful photography!<br/></td>', 'Awesome, Enzo!  It is a beautiful photo.  The kind that stirs my heart and the kind of photography that I am passionate about.  But it is even a more beautiful story of what you are doing in the Philippines.  I sponsor an "adopted" little girl in the Philippines that I''ve been supporting since she was 3, and she''s almost old enough to be graduated from the program now, so I always have had a special interest in the Philippines, and wish someday I could go there myself.   I''m glad you won first place with this wonderful photography!', '2009-03-23 09:42:30.000000', NULL, 0),
