(5396454, 773830, 50034, '<td valign="top">SOL to me!  This is what I get for trying to out-think the voters!<br/> <br/>Sadly, the way I have post-processed this photograph makes it appear that the colors are running!  This certainly was not my desire...obviously, but past experience tells me that "blown-out" whites get lower scores.<br/> <br/>4.55 over-all means that the background didn''t need color to prevent a lower score.  Undesirable effect, and a less-than-pleasant impact.<br/> <br/>Thank You for not being any more harsh than you were...  :/</td>', 'SOL to me!  This is what I get for trying to out-think the voters! Sadly, the way I have post-processed this photograph makes it appear that the colors are running!  This certainly was not my desire...obviously, but past experience tells me that "blown-out" whites get lower scores. 4.55 over-all means that the background didn''t need color to prevent a lower score.  Undesirable effect, and a less-than-pleasant impact. Thank You for not being any more harsh than you were...  :/', '2009-03-23 11:03:13.000000', NULL, 0),
