(5399570, 773444, 30807, '<td valign="top">Lovely photo - I can imagine the children''s reactions - the parents must have loved them too. What church is it? Are you a Latter-Day Saint? What do you do with all the photos you take - I wondered if it for the Church''s humanitarian efforts. I know the Gospel changes people - I suppose it is true that the World''s way is to take people out of the slums, but the Gospel takes the slums out of the people, who then take themselves out of the slums. My concern is always a worry that the nice expensive camera with which I photograph a bad situation might have been better used to improve the situation of the person photographed, but then, who would know about the bad situation? I come down on the side of photographing the situation, and then the response of the viewer can bring in more than the cost of the camera, and more people can help. If you let me know what church, I would be interested to help. You can send a private email for contact details if needed, of course. Anyway, beautiful shot, lovely exposure, good spirit on the day, I can see.<br/> <br/>Many more awards for you, I am sure.</td>', 'Lovely photo - I can imagine the children''s reactions - the parents must have loved them too. What church is it? Are you a Latter-Day Saint? What do you do with all the photos you take - I wondered if it for the Church''s humanitarian efforts. I know the Gospel changes people - I suppose it is true that the World''s way is to take people out of the slums, but the Gospel takes the slums out of the people, who then take themselves out of the slums. My concern is always a worry that the nice expensive camera with which I photograph a bad situation might have been better used to improve the situation of the person photographed, but then, who would know about the bad situation? I come down on the side of photographing the situation, and then the response of the viewer can bring in more than the cost of the camera, and more people can help. If you let me know what church, I would be interested to help. You can send a private email for contact details if needed, of course. Anyway, beautiful shot, lovely exposure, good spirit on the day, I can see. Many more awards for you, I am sure.', '2009-03-25 06:10:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(5399596, 773831, 30807, '<td valign="top">Gosh - well rescued from the original - I feel you captured in the title the hope that you wouldn''t get mugged by late-night problem people. Looks just like Middlesbrough or many other cities at night. Very good choice of image, and completely on-target with the feeling. I like the warmer colour of the treatment, and the improved dynamics. <br/> <br/>Well done!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Gosh - well rescued from the original - I feel you captured in the title the hope that you wouldn''t get mugged by late-night problem people. Looks just like Middlesbrough or many other cities at night. Very good choice of image, and completely on-target with the feeling. I like the warmer colour of the treatment, and the improved dynamics.  Well done! ', '2009-03-25 06:42:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(5400018, 771834, 29011, '<td valign="top">This easily made my top10. My favorite of your recent reptile pics :)  The frog eggs have a cool texture and I concur with other comments, great color! and composition.</td>', 'This easily made my top10. My favorite of your recent reptile pics :)  The frog eggs have a cool texture and I concur with other comments, great color! and composition.', '2009-03-25 10:17:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(5400161, 773821, 67697, '<td valign="top">This is interesting - it''s almost like a dark Alice-in-Wonderland kind of story.  I''m not sure if I am sold on the bluish tint but I love the processing.  Love the drama - her face makes you want to know what is going on here.</td>', 'This is interesting - it''s almost like a dark Alice-in-Wonderland kind of story.  I''m not sure if I am sold on the bluish tint but I love the processing.  Love the drama - her face makes you want to know what is going on here.', '2009-03-25 11:27:28.000000', NULL, 0),
